{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778941470,"nonce":"muvi4DmZHPnG9UKweykF/bvWxFM=","message":"## Child issue split and recommended gate order\n\nI split the ledger work into gated implementation issues so this does not become one unreviewable backend/UI rewrite.\n\nRecommended order:\n\n1. ff6a2bc — Ledger core: schema, project identity, events, outbox, backups.\n   - Build the canonical substrate in shadow mode without behavior cutover.\n2. aac782a — Ledger git-bug adapter: import/export, labels, cursors, conflicts.\n   - Make git-bug a first-class compatibility mirror with idempotency and conflict records.\n3. 59d527a — Ledger migration gate: shadow reconciliation and issue API cutover.\n   - Compare ledger projections against current scanner output and prevent split-brain cutover.\n4. e8c1d43 — Ledger integration: work units, auth requests, sessions, commits.\n   - Move operational joins to canonical ledger issue IDs while preserving compatibility fields.\n5. b45f19b — Graph projection: ledger relationships, deterministic layouts, live overlays.\n   - Rebase graph structure on ledger relationships and clearer auth/session semantics.\n6. 23b67b7 — Ledger UI: issue detail, comments, sync/conflict UX.\n   - Make the ledger inspectable and actionable from the Issues and Graph surfaces.\n7. dotfiles 3b9f763 — Global conventions for Mandible ledger-era issue tracking.\n   - Update agent instructions when the concrete ledger-era commands/trailers/fallbacks settle.\n\nAll Mandible child issues have `parent:097d2b7`. I also added the `umbrella` label to this issue.\n\nThe key gate is that route/CLI write cutover must not happen before import/export, outbox processing, adapter cursors, and conflict records exist. Graph/UI work should consume stable ledger contracts, but it should not force the ledger core and migration cutover into one protected-branch merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}